# Google's Gemini CLI as a kiln harness in a Shards microVM (kiln plan
# 01a1cd8e862e7169a074db3d5fa33f3d, step 21; plan 01a1ce705e2374dfbac201fe6ba98184, research
# 01a1ce705e2472df9f3dd81be0531c9f). kiln runs it as its ACP server, `gemini --acp` (Kind "gemini",
# crates/kiln/src/harness/kinds.rs; f17). It comes in as pin.json pins it, in ./gemini-<arch>/:
# Google's npm package, its registry signatures and SHA-512 checked by pin.sh, unpacked with its
# package/ directory stripped; node/bin/node and node/LICENSE from Node.js's own Linux build, whose
# SHA-256 Node's signed SHASUMS256.txt gives; and kiln's harness.json and system-settings.json.
# Nothing else installs it, and no credential is in the image.

# Google ships no Linux executable of Gemini CLI: its Linux build is the npm package, run by Node.js 20
# or later (f5, f6). Node's Linux builds link glibc (2.28 at most), libstdc++ and libgcc_s (f12), and
# Node publishes no arm64 musl build (f11): the base needs glibc, and bash for Gemini's shell tool
# (f26), and the image has no libc variant. This default, step 19's, pinned by digest, has them all and
# runs the harness with no RUN (f13); Alpine can't start it.
ARG BASE=buildpack-deps:trixie-scm@sha256:4f34e1d673fdb65371de9f88bdd32c4e30152fe692b35604aef5c0b3c0e6da10
FROM ${BASE}

# BuildKit sets TARGETARCH in the global scope, so the stage declares it to name each platform's
# harness directory.
ARG TARGETARCH
HARNESS gemini FROM ./gemini-${TARGETARCH}

# Its network, every part named (default deny; Shards D236, destinations by name): a network for this
# harness alone, which it joins with no flow to any member, and TCP out to the hosts below alone, by
# name, through the network's boundary (--egress) and the microVM's (EXPOSE ... AS egress). Each name
# resolves for it through the agents' resolver, and no other does. Nothing comes in; no other host,
# port or protocol goes out. 443 is HTTPS's port (RFC 9110 4.2.2). Each host is cited to its vendor's own
# documentation, or, where that names a wildcard or nothing, to the vendor's own source or build, in its
# harness's record's "Hosts by name" (kiln plan 01a1cd8e862e7169a074db3d5fa33f3d, step 18, part 4):
# docs/research/s21-gemini-agentfile/README.md, each from Google's own documentation and the pinned build's source:
# - cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com: Code Assist, where a Google sign-in's turns go (Google's Gemini Code Assist network
#   page; code_assist/server.ts at v0.68.0).
# - generativelanguage.googleapis.com: the Gemini API, signed in with a key (the Gemini API reference; @google/genai).
# - oauth2.googleapis.com: Google's token endpoint, a sign-in's refresh and its check that a token isn't revoked (Google's
#   OAuth docs for desktop apps; google-auth-library).
# - www.googleapis.com: the signed-in account's user info (Google's OAuth2 API definition; oauth2.ts).
# Its usage statistics (play.googleapis.com), Vertex AI's regional hosts and npm's update check (off, f23) go nowhere.
# kiln's MCP isn't granted here, nor in any of kiln's Agentfiles: it reaches the harness over the link
# kiln drives it by, as that link's own `mcp` lane (Shards D254), never over the network.
NETWORK --egress=cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com:443 --egress=generativelanguage.googleapis.com:443 --egress=oauth2.googleapis.com:443 --egress=www.googleapis.com:443 provider FOR gemini
EXPOSE --harnesses=gemini 443/tcp AS egress FOR provider
CONNECT gemini WITH gemini ON provider

# Its project is plugged in as it starts, at the path it has on the machine (Shards D235), so kiln
# reads its diffs, HEAD and checkpoints at that same path, and no volume holds it. Its HOME is the
# person's volume, whole: harness.json sets HOME=/home/gemini, kiln's one rule for every harness it
# ships (step 18). A harness sees its image read-only, with its own /tmp scratch, so a HOME that is
# writable and kept from run to run is a volume, and what the programs it runs keep in a home (a
# .gitconfig, a tool's sign-in) is kept with it. Gemini CLI keeps its settings, its sign-in, its
# history, its projects and their memory under $HOME/.gemini (f20, f21).
# HOME in run.env needs a shards at or after 997f4e47e (v0.8.0 and later), where run.env replaces
# init's HOME=/tmp. The volume is the harness's alone, and outside /tmp, which the scratch covers.
VOLUME --target-kind=harness /home/gemini FOR gemini
